/* book exam traps: Linear-regulator loss is (Vin − Vo)·Io, not Vin·Io. Using Vin·Io counts the useful output power as heat. | SMPS efficiency is Po/Pin. Vo/Vin is meaningless for a switcher, which can step up or step down. | Dropout is a voltage difference, not a current. Below Vo + dropout the regulator cannot hold regulation. | A higher switching frequency shrinks the magnetics but does not automatically raise efficiency; switching loss and EMI grow. */
